-- title:
--   Descent by one prime: j(q^M)∈ℚ(j(q),j(q^{Mp}))
-- statement:
--   Fix a nonzero natural number $M$ and a prime $p$, and let $K$ be a field equipped with a $\mathbb{Q}$-algebra structure together with a unit $\zeta\in K^\times$ whose underlying element is a primitive $(Mp)$-th root of unity. Write $\mathrm{jq}\in\mathbb{Q}((q))$ for the Laurent series $q^{-1}$ times the rational $j$-numerator power series, and for $N\neq 0$ let $\mathrm{jqN}\,N$ be its image under the substitution $q\mapsto q^{N}$ (the ring endomorphism `qExpand` of Laurent series raising exponents by the factor $N$). Let $P$ be the polynomial over $K((q))$ obtained from the minimal polynomial of $\mathrm{jqN}\,M$ over the intermediate field $\mathbb{Q}(\mathrm{jq})\subseteq\mathbb{Q}((q))$ by applying to each coefficient the inclusion into $\mathbb{Q}((q))$, then the substitution $q\mapsto q^{Mp}$, then the coefficientwise map $\mathbb{Q}\to K$. Two hypotheses are imposed on the roots of $P$ in $K((q))$: first, if $y$ is a root and $y=\mathrm{jq}$ rescaled by $q\mapsto q^{M^{2}p}$ and twisted by a unit $w\in K^\times$ (the twist multiplying the coefficient of $q^{k}$ by $w^{k}$), then $w=1$; second, no root of $P$ equals the image in $K((q))$ of $\mathrm{jqN}(Mp^{2})$ rescaled by $q\mapsto q^{Mp}$. The conclusion is that $\mathrm{jqN}\,M$ lies in the intermediate field of $\mathbb{Q}((q))$ generated over $\mathbb{Q}$ by $\mathrm{jq}$ and $\mathrm{jqN}(Mp)$.
--
--   This is the descent step in the purely algebraic determination of the field generated by the $q$-expansions of $j$ and $j_N$: passing from level $Mp$ down to level $M$, $j(q^{M})$ is recovered as the unique common root of the level-$p$ modular equation evaluated at $j(q^{Mp})$ and of the minimal polynomial of $j(q^{M})$ over $\mathbb{Q}(j)$. It feeds the generation statement $\mathbb{Q}(j,j_N)$ for the function field of $X_0(N)$ and the computation of $[\mathbb{Q}(j)(j_N):\mathbb{Q}(j)]=\psi(N)$, i.e. irreducibility of the modular polynomial $\Phi_N$ over $\mathbb{Q}(j)$.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_jqN_div_mem_modularFunctionField.lean

